  "dom_id": "step-q237318",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14190698/assets/633e75b1b02b1eba8f512af09a88d7e671da2b238828529ace0a216688f48dd0.png)\n\nGiven that $\\overset{―}{AD}$ is a segment, what is the measure of $∠BOD?$",
  "worked_solution": "Two angles are supplementary if their measures add up to ${180}^{∘},$ a straight angle.\n\nSince $\\overset{―}{AD}$ is a segment, we have that $∠BOA$ and $∠BOD$ are supplementary. \n\n$$\nm∠BOA+m∠BOD={180}^{∘}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of $∠BOD$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠BOD & ={180}^{∘}-m∠BOA \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{132}^{∘} \\\\  & ={48}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
